    "summary": "What Web Rabbit Payments is and how the API is structured.",
    "text": "export default function Introduction() {\n return (\n <>\n \n The Web Rabbit Payments API lets you accept Mobile Money and card payments in Ghana with\n a single integration. You get one API, one dashboard, and one settlement — we handle the rails.\n\n Overview \n \n The API is organised around REST. It uses predictable resource-oriented URLs, accepts JSON-encoded\n request bodies, returns JSON-encoded responses, and uses standard HTTP response codes and verbs.\n\n Base URL \n All endpoints are served over HTTPS at: \n / \n \n There is no separate host to call. The mode of the request ( test or \n live ) is determined by the key prefix: wr_test_... runs against the\n provider's sandbox environment, wr_live_... hits production rails. Test and live data\n are fully isolated.\n\n Health check \n \n GET / /health is unauthenticated and returns \n with HTTP \n 200 . Use it for uptime monitoring — it is still subject to the unauthenticated per-IP\n rate limit.\n\n Payment providers \n \n Behind the API we settle through licensed Ghanaian payment providers — 360Pay\n (LibertePay) and JuniPay . Each business is routed to one of them; the\n routing is managed by us and never changes your request or response shape. The normalised \n status ( approved · pending · failed ) is\n identical either way — only the raw code and reason passed through from\n upstream differ. See \n Provider codes .\n\n POST /v1/payout/momo and /v1/payout/bank are retired and return \n 501 provider_unsupported . Withdrawals are requested from \n Payouts in the merchant dashboard and settled by our operations team.\n\n Test mode & Live mode \n \n Every business has two independent environments. Live mode unlocks after your\n business is approved and processes real payments.\n\n wr_test_ keys make real API calls to the provider's sandbox environment — name\n verification runs first, the collection is accepted as pending , and the outcome is\n delivered by the provider's settlement callback. No real money moves, and no outcome is faked. See \n Test data .\n\n You can create live API keys, but charges will fail until your business status is approved .\n Complete verification from the Verification page.\n\n Only GHS is supported today. Amounts are decimal (e.g. 10.50 ) — we\n handle any pesewa-string conversion required by upstream rails.\n\n Ready to charge your first customer? \n Jump to the Quickstart → \n \n )\n}"
