    "title": "Mobile Money",
    "summary": "Charge a customer over MTN, Telecel, or AirtelTigo.",
    "text": "export default function CollectMomo() {\n return (\n <>\n \n Charge a customer over Mobile Money. The customer receives a prompt on their phone to authorise the\n payment, so the charge always starts as pending and settles asynchronously.\n\n The API key must have write access. Read-only keys receive \n 403 insufficient_scope .\n\n Endpoint \n\n Pass the network field using one of these codes: MTN · \n TELECEL (formerly Vodafone) · AT (AirtelTigo) · GMONEY .\n Legacy codes VDF , ATL and TGO are still accepted and mapped\n automatically. See \n institution codes .\n\n subscriber_number accepts either the local format 0240000000 or the\n international format 233240000000 — we normalise it for the provider. \n amount is decimal GHS — no pesewa padding. See \n test numbers .\n\n Before any debit we run the provider's mandatory name lookup on the wallet. If the number cannot be\n resolved you get 422 account_not_found and no transaction is created .\n On success the resolved account_name is returned and stored with the transaction.\n This applies to both upstream providers; the lookup wording in reason differs between\n 360Pay and JuniPay.\n\n If the provider accepts the request shape but refuses the charge, the transaction is recorded as \n failed and the endpoint answers 502 with the provider's own reason in \n reason . Retry with the same Idempotency-Key .\n\n Request \n\n Send an Idempotency-Key header to make retries safe — see \n Idempotency .\n\n true,\n CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER => true,\n CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER => [\n \"Authorization: Bearer wr_test_...\",\n \"Content-Type: application/json\",\n \"Idempotency-Key: 8f4b7c1e-invoice-a104\",\n ],\n CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS => json_encode([\n \"amount\" => 10.50,\n \"subscriber_number\" => \"0240000000\",\n \"network\" => \"MTN\",\n \"desc\" => \"Invoice A104\",\n \"customer_email\" => \"customer@example.com\",\n ]),\n]);\n$tx = json_decode(curl_exec($ch), true);\necho $tx[\"transaction_id\"]; ,\n },\n ]}\n />\n\n Response \n\n 202 for pending (the usual case — the customer still has to authorise on their phone),\n 201 if the provider settles immediately, 200 for a resolved failure, \n 422 when the wallet fails name verification. All responses include an \n x-request-id header — save it if you need support. The final outcome is confirmed by \n polling the retrieve endpoint .\n\n wr_test_ keys run against the provider's UAT environment — real API calls, no real\n money. Use the sandbox wallet from \n Test data .\n\n )\n}"
